            "text_89QDy6": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Many women describe brain fog during perimenopause: trouble concentrating, forgetfulness, or struggling to find the right word. Estrogen plays a role in how the brain uses energy and in memory and attention, so as levels fluctuate, thinking can feel slower or less sharp.</p><p>Poor sleep, hot flashes and stress add to the effect. Research suggests that for most women these changes are temporary and tend to improve after the menopause transition. It is not a sign that something is permanently wrong.</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
