            "text_KwEnHH": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Everyday steps.</strong> Many women get real relief from simple changes:</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": false,
                "line_height": 26,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 0,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_NGe8XV": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<ul><li>Prioritize sleep. Even modest improvements in sleep can noticeably sharpen focus and memory.</li><li>Use lists, calendars and routines to take the load off your memory, and tackle demanding tasks at the time of day you feel clearest.</li><li>Stay physically active and socially engaged. Regular exercise supports blood flow to the brain and overall cognitive health.</li></ul>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": true,
                "line_height": 36,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 0,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_mAtczE": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Products that may help.</strong> Some women find hormone-free supplements helpful, though the evidence is mixed and quality varies. We stock a small selection chosen for manufacturing quality, and we show the evidence level on every product page. Supplements are not FDA-approved to treat any condition, and what works for one woman may do nothing for another.</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": false,
                "line_height": 26,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 20,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_wejyc7": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>When to see a clinician.</strong> If memory problems are getting worse, affect your ability to work or manage daily life, or people close to you are noticing changes, talk to a clinician. They can check for other causes such as thyroid problems, low B12, medication side effects or depression. Bacton does not prescribe; we can help you prepare for that conversation.</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
